WEBVTT

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.990
This moron is an amazing guy.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.280
Even though he’s in this state...

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.740
He just can’t seem to give up on making something delicious to save you.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.330
You must do your best, Kanmuri...

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.460
Thank you, Azuma-kun.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.710
I was about to give up, but thanks to you
it looks like I’m stirred up once again.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.630
But...

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.470
The flaming jam that my opponent is going to be making, jam flambe, is a first-class jam.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.970
If I lose after having tried my
very best, please forgive me.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.230
What’s with this room? Doesn’t it kinda stink?

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.020
That’s true...

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.190
It could be coming from the firewood.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.200
There are certain varieties of trees
that give off a strange smell when burnt.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:53.780
I got it!

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.240
What’s with you all of a sudden?

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.080
I got it!

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.450
The best idea!

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.620
You must do your best, Kanmuri...

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.290
Thank you Azuma-kun.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.960
This is also thanks to you.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.420
That’s right.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.380
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.260
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.550
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.950
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:25.060
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.690
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:39.540
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:45.710
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:02:00.850
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:09.400
probably helped me notice that

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:15.320
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:24.170
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:29.580
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:36.680
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:42.510
that white sky with my colors.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:49.520
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.860
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.420
The sibling showdown!!

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.760
The first-class man chosen by Dad!

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:11.860
Oh?

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.030
Masanobu...

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.250
Well, would you look at that. You have come to observe us?

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.500
My cute little sons are going to be in a match.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.750
As a father, I felt that I must see it through.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.960
Cute little sons indeed.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:30.300
It’s not like you came to any of our sports meets or parent-participation sessions.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.770
But now that it’s down to deciding who
becomes your successor, you come, huh?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.020
I’m sorry, Masanobu.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.650
Due to my being in this fateful position,

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.490
I’ve caused you boys a lot of trouble.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.780
If you’ve said all you wanted to,

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.000
would you please head to the audience
stands and conduct yourself quietly?

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.750
Boss, is it all right like this?

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:52.960
Aoyagi...

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:53.500
Yes?

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.880
I’m still not sure about this.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:56.540
Huh?

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.380
Masanobu, the Austrian court chef...

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.220
And Shigeru, a graduate of the Harvard University Food Sciences Research Institute...

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:07.010
Both are first-class men who have
succeeded at wholesome paths.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:12.020
I don’t know if it’s good to
pull them forcibly into our world.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.310
I understand how you feel, but...

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:19.360
unfortunately, we don’t have any talented
people in our group to take over instead.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.400
And that includes me...

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.620
Our group is said to have
tens of thousands of underlings,

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:34.660
and in order to keep them from being turned out
to the streets, a first-class man must be made boss.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.170
A first-class man, huh?

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.300
Truth be told, Kanmuri-kun...

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:48.680
I don’t really care whether or not
I inherit after the old man.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.600
Because your mother gave birth to you...

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.190
my mother and I were driven out of the Hashiguchi home.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:00.650
After that, all we heard of were
stories of what a genius you were.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.050
Before I knew it,

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:07.700
the feelings of jealousy and hatred I bore against you were growing uncontrollably.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.370
The time for me to surpass you has finally...

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.790
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.960
You’re late, Kanmuri.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.540
You should come with time to spare.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.130
I’m sorry.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.720
But, I really needed it to win today’s match.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:27.720
This apple tree log.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.600
And it took me a while to find the perfect log, so...

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:32.770
I’m sorry.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.140
Whatever.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.430
Get ready at once.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.020
It’s true that the sweet and sour flavor of rhubarb
goes well with the sweet and sour flavor of apples.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:45.490
But, that’s only when you mix in
the actual fruit or the fruit juice.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:48.750
What the hell do you think you’ll accomplish
by bringing the damn tree along?

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.450
Very well, we will now begin the fifth match
of Yakitate!! 9 here in Shinanomachi.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.370
Begin!

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.380
Aoyagi...

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.930
Masanobu seems to be using a black, round pot.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.300
What in the world is that?

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.680
I wouldn’t know...

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.350
I-It’s you!

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:18.230
Get ready to face the
consequences of your earlier actions!

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.770
What idiots.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.280
To think that you’d cast away
your lives, which I once spared...

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.480
Who is that man?

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.350
That is the baker I was speaking of earlier,

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:30.070
working at the store where
Master Shigeru is employed.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:31.280
Oh?

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.120
That’s him?

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:33.700
L-Like that matters!

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:34.950
Everyone, get him!

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.000
All right!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.120
Stop that.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:38.920
Idiots.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:42.090
Don’t I always tell you not to
unnecessarily attack civilians?

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:43.640
We’re very sorry.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:49.220
It appears we have caused you some trouble.
Sorry about that.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.730
Not really.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:53.350
Not so much trouble that you’d need to apologize.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:54.690
Is that so?

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:57.070
In that case, I have a favor to ask of you.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:00.150
What?

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:02.520
You want me to explain the match to you?

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:03.660
That’s right.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:08.870
At this rate, I am completely unable to
understand how my sons’ match is proceeding.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.790
Can I not ask this of you?

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:11.790
Don’t wanna.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:12.790
No, huh?

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.240
Too much of a pain.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.290
Meanie!

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:17.710
Manager...

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.500
Isn’t it all right?

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:25.260
I think that it’s wonderful that he wishes
to understand his sons’ match properly.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:27.390
Whatever.

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:28.760
Fine, I’ll explain.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.430
Just remember this.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.810
Even if Kanmuri is to lose this match,

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:42.110
if you try to force him into becoming
boss of your group, you’ll have to face me.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.950
What a man.

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:49.620
He’s picking a fight with me, knowing full well
that I’m the head of the Hashiguchi group.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:50.910
Well then.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:52.620
Listen carefully.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.820
That blackish, round pot that Tsutsumi is about to use

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:58.130
is probably made of volcanic rock.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:01.300
Volcanic rock emits far-infrared rays.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:05.380
Therefore, when used as a pot
to boil jam, it is the perfect item.

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:10.140
He’s going to use that to make warm jam.

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:11.390
Warm jam?

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.970
The reason marketed jams
are refrigerated

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.560
is simply because it’s convenient to preserve them that way.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.610
Normally, jam is more delicious when warm.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.520
Is that so?

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:21.100
I wouldn’t know...

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.770
That is why it’s the most basic of jam fundamentals

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.610
to come up with a good way
to warm jam up.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:34.870
In that case, if would be more delicious to warm
jam up before spreading it on bread at home.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.370
You’d think so, right?

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.290
Indeed.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:39.290
But that’s not what happens in reality.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.380
Wh-Why not?

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:46.340
Depending on whether it’s warm or cold, the
strength of the same food item’s taste can change.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:51.010
It’s like how cold fruit juice feels
too sweet to drink when warm.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:56.390
The sweet-taste sensors of human
beings sense sweetness the most

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:59.440
at temperatures close to body temperature.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:03.150
If you warm up refrigerated jam...

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.980
Like juice, you would find that it is too sweet?

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.480
That’s right.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:11.480
The world of cooking is deep indeed.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.360
Deep, you say?!

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:14.870
Kawachi-san!

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.790
What about the match?

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.870
After all, Azuma-san is unable to participate this time.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:22.380
Like I’ve said before, the true commander always...

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:22.840
Oh, it looks like Tsutsumi-san is up to something!
Like I’ve said before, the true commander always...

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.960
Oh, it looks like Tsutsumi-san is up to something!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:25.960
You’re just gonna ignore me all of a sudden?!

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:27.880
Well then.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.220
I guess it’s time to finish up.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:30.970
I’ll get this done in one go!

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:35.140
A flambe, huh?

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:36.480
Flambe?

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.850
It’s a technique where you splash on liquor high in alcohol content

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:41.940
and set fire to it to produce a strong fragrance.

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:46.730
Indeed, even though we’re so far away,
a wonderful fragrance is wafting our way.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.450
Very impressive, Masanobu.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:53.780
You have mastered the ultimate technique that
can move even complete amateurs like me.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:54.740
Of course.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:56.620
All right, it’s done.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.420
Mr. Judge.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:01.880
I request that you sample my item.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.400
The alcohol is burning,

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.710
but the temperature of the actual jam should be all right for consumption.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.010
This is very dangerous
Please do not imitate it at any cost!

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:14.300
He put his face into the flaming pot!
This is very dangerous
Please do not imitate it at any cost!

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.730
What meaning is there in doing something like that?

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:18.560
Geez.

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:20.440
You call yourself the big boss of the baddies,

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:22.900
but it seems you can’t understand the true essence of things at all.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:24.010
Wh-Wh... What?!

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:25.690
Listen up.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:28.940
If you look at things with only your eyes,
you cannot understand their true nature.

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:31.780
You must look at it with the mind’s eye.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.530
Look... Look at it with my mind’s eye...

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.240
Th-This is...

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.750
I-I can see it!

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.420
The superhero of all children.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:47.000
The warrior of justice made of sweet bean jam!

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:48.010
That’s right.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.210
That’s the spirit.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:53.470
So, who is it that makes that superhero?

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:54.260
The manga artist?!

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:55.600
You idiot!

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.680
I’m not talking about something
remotely close to reality!

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:59.390
Look at his head!

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:00.480
H-Head...?

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.980
D-Don’t tell me...

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.650
The person making the superhero is...

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:07.320
That’s right!

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.730
The real person making him is...

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.070
Uncle Jam!

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.790
K... Kuro-yan is impressive as always.

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:31.670
That guy’s got some guts.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.880
Of course.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.590
He’s a professional judge.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:37.800
He would give up his life to express
the deliciousness of something.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:40.810
That was wonderful jam, Tsutsumi.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:44.550
This is something that can be called
ultimate among ultimate jams.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:51.060
In addition to using volcanic rock as a pot to make warm jam...

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:56.900
The item you used to make the flambe is a gem amongst gems.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.950
This is the crimson jewel, calvados.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.240
It’s just as you say.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.450
This is apple brandy made from the variety of apple known as “crimson jewel”

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:08.960
by allowing it to ferment for 10 years.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.840
While making flambe, the most important
thing to keep in mind is the fragrance.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:19.680
That is why I judged that the calvados, with
its mellow fragrance, is most suitable for it.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:22.600
A superb choice.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.180
I, Kuroyanagi, am impressed.

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:27.140
How’s that, Kanmuri-kun?

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.270
I’ve used various traditional
techniques to their full extent...

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.980
to create the ultimate jam that surpasses all others.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.230
You no longer have any hope of winning.

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:39.070
So many different strategies...

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:42.370
I guess we can be certain that Masanobu has won.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.830
This is why amateurs are troublesome.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:50.420
Kanmuri is so amazing that no one would believe he’s your son.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.580
He won’t be put down with just this.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:56.590
Then, you say that he has a secret plan that will help him surpass that wonderful jam?

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:58.050
Of course.

00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:59.300
That’s what the apple tree log is for.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:01.590
You mean that?

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:05.100
But even then,
isn’t that just a piece of wood?

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:07.350
What in the world is he going to use it for?

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:08.850
I just...

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:09.850
don’t know.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.400
You don’t know?

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:14.110
But aren’t you Shigeru’s friend?

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:15.860
Well, I think so, but...

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.610
Then, why don’t you know...?

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:18.740
Hey, what are you trying to say?

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:24.200
That just because you’re friends with all your
underlings here, you know <i>all</i> their secrets?

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:26.950
Don’t pay him any attention.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:28.910
He’s just that kind of person.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:29.960
Yup.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.080
Wh-What’s that...?

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:38.010
C-Could it be a fire?!

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:38.710
Boss!

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:40.590
Hurry up and put out the fire!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:41.970
We must save Shigeru!

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:42.680
Yes sir!

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:46.560
Don’t butt in!

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.640
You plan on destroying a high-level match like this?

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.850
Wh-What do you mean?

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:54.270
Even I only figured it out just now...

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:55.940
What Kanmuri’s true intent is.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.610
Shigeru’s true intent?

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.650
That is one of the techniques used for smoking.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.610
A technique called hot smoking.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:07.360
In other words, he’s using the
apple tree wood to smoke the jam.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.240
S-Smoking?

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:11.580
Is that why there is so much smoke?

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:12.960
Look at the monitor.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:19.460
He’s burning the apple tree wood inside the drum canister to smoke the jam.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:20.960
B-But...

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:23.670
Would jam taste good upon being smoked?

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:28.720
You’d be able to warm it up, but
wouldn’t a strange smell stick to it...?

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:30.270
Don’t be stupid.

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.980
Take in the fragrance of this smoke properly.

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:34.940
The fragrance of the smoke...?

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:38.940
This sweet fragrance is that of apples...?

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:44.240
The chips used for smoking come from cherry trees,
the Japanese bead tree, chestnut trees, etc.

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:49.120
When you want to smoke items
like jam that need to be sweet,

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.950
apple trees are known to be the best.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.040
Masanobu’s flambe...

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:55.620
And Shigeru’s smoked jam...

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:57.920
The world of cooking is fearsome.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.670
What a wonderful world.

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:04.260
Looks like you’ve gone and done it, Kanmuri-kun.

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:07.390
To think that you could use apple tree wood like this...

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.180
But...

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:12.640
My jam flambe was ultimate among ultimate jams.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:16.560
No matter what strategy you use, it is
impossible for it to lose to other jams.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:21.070
I’ve heard that the judge is a
former Pantasia member, but...

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.440
Looking at his skill earlier,

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:27.570
I know that he is a first-class person who will not bring personal feelings into the match.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:30.950
I’m sure that he will announce my victory.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:36.710
All right.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:37.420
It looks good.

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:39.420
Looks like it’s done.

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:39.920
Yeah.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.880
It’s done.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.630
Kuroyanagi-senp... I mean Mr. Judge...

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:46.750
No matter what the item may be,

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.800
a faintly astringent taste is left in it upon being smoked, but...

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:53.140
I’ve heard that doesn’t happen
when you use apple tree wood.

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:57.640
Looks like I must steel myself for this.

00:15:58.860 --> 00:15:59.440
All right then.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:11.950
Look!

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.240
There’s no reaction!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:18.040
After having tasted my jam, it’s obvious
that any other jam would fail in comparison!

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:27.590
No, that’s not it!

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:29.680
He’s entered a trance!

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:32.760
I must assume that he’s preparing for some reaction!

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:34.810
What is it?

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.510
What in the world is he looking for?

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:41.560
Oh no!

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.650
S-Stop that!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.070
Tsu-Tsutsumi-san!

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.450
What’s with him?

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:54.330
Looks like he tried to interfere with Kuro-yan’s
reaction when it looked like he’d lose.

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:55.330
Like hell that’d work.

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:57.120
L-Like hell I did.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.080
Someone stop that judge!

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:00.580
Masanobu!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.790
We’re in the middle of the judging of Shigeru’s jam here.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.300
You cannot possibly interfere with the judging process.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:07.710
No! It’s just as he says!

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:09.170
We must stop Kuroyanagi!

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.800
Wh-What’s with you, Manager?

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.850
Don’t you get it yet?

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:18.100
At this rate, Kuro-yan’s gonna enter
that drum canister and smoke himself!

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:19.690
What was that?!

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:23.060
If he were to enter that, it
wouldn’t end at just Uncle Jam.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:23.810
Stop him!

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:24.440
Yes sir!

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:31.240
Don’t get in my... way!

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:31.910
He’s really strong despite his slender body.
Don’t get in my... way!

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.740
He’s really strong despite his slender body.

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:38.540
His passion toward his reactions are higher than a mountain and deeper than the seas.

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:40.250
He can’t be stopped that easily!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.880
Isn’t there a way to stop him?

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:43.880
There’s just one way.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:44.790
What’s that?

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:45.790
Tsukino.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.090
Become a fortuneteller.

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:47.960
Huh?

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:51.090
Become a fortuneteller and tell Kuroyanagi’s fortune.

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:53.340
Manager!

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.180
What you’re saying makes no sense!

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:55.430
Understood.
What you’re saying makes no sense!

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:56.600
It made sense?

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:00.270
Wh-What do you plan on doing?

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:01.810
Tsukino! Attack!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.730
Roger!

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:08.650
I will read your fortune.

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:10.240
Fortune?!

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:12.740
He changed directions!

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:13.950
Just watch.

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:14.700
Now!

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:19.330
What does this mean?

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:21.080
Why did he change directions?

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:23.120
It is a compensatory reaction.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.370
Compensatory reaction?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.960
When the first action you wanted to perform cannot occur,

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:31.970
in order to comfort yourself, you
pick something else that you like to do.

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:33.380
This is a compensatory reaction.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:37.370
In other words, by asking the girl to tell a fortune,

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:40.430
you prevented him from smoking himself?

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:41.390
That’s right.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:47.360
But, right now he’s not heading to
the fortunetelling girl, but to the..

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:53.700
Monkey bars?!

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.200
Don’t tell me...

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:02.870
Monkey bars! Is that so?!

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:04.160
Is that it?!

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:08.790
What a man.

00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:12.970
In addition to his valor and complete lack of
fear of me, the boss of the Hashiguchi group...

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:17.550
there’s his ability to assess situations that
helps resolve crises like these in no time.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:22.680
If you don’t call this man first class,
you cannot call anyone first class.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.350
What’s with him?!

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.810
Wait just a moment.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:31.190
What happened to the all-important win or loss?

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.820
Very impressive Kanmuri.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:37.820
You preserved the flavor of the rhubarb 100%
by using the freeze-concentration technique.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:40.740
In addition, your strategy of
smoking it using apple tree wood.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:45.210
This also enters the class of
ultimate among ultimate jams.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.790
Therefore this match is...

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.800
Devoid of winners.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.040
A... A draw?!

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:59.760
Yep, at times when I cannot discriminate,
the match is declared a draw.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:01.260
N-No way...

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.930
Then the problem of the successor...

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:03.810
What are you going to do about it?

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:05.770
I’ll do it.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.940
Ma-Masanobu...

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.020
Tsutsumi-san!

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.940
No matter how you looked at it,

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:17.030
I, being the Austrian court chef, was at
an advantage when it came to making jam.

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:19.240
While the result may have been a draw...

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:21.030
I have no choice but to admit my defeat.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.990
No, please wait Tsutsumi-san!

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:25.950
In that case, it is just too...

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:26.910
It’s all right.

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:31.290
I’ve come to terms with everything,
having fought you with everything I had.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.290
Tsutsumi-san.

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:35.380
And I’ve given up as a cook.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.800
Don’t lie!

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.800
Your feelings of loving to cook are the real thing.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:46.310
Anyone who saw how you desperately tried to stop
Kuroyanagi’s reaction would know that immediately.

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:50.400
It’s because you didn’t want someone who understood
the taste of true culinary masterpieces to die...

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:52.310
that you did it.

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:53.570
Right?

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:56.530
Hey Manager...

00:20:56.530 --> 00:21:00.240
Just when it looked like we could push off
the problem of the successor onto him...

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:01.530
Just shut up!
Just when it looked like we could push off
the problem of the successor onto him...

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:04.240
No, but I...

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.540
It’s all right now.

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:06.580
Masanobu...

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.040
And Shigeru.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:09.500
Dad...

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:13.040
You no longer have to worry about who will succeed.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.750
I was wrong.

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:19.680
The world of cooking has immeasurable depths...

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:23.970
I can’t make people like you, who can have a high-level match like this in this world,

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.760
succeed someone like me.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:29.940
B-Boss!

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:31.690
In that case who’ll take care of our group?

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:33.610
Don’t worry.

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:36.480
I found us the perfect successor.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.900
That is... this man!

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:45.910
We can have no complaints about this man’s appearance or personality.

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:47.160
He is very skilled, too.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:50.790
In addition, he has a great ability to assess situations and is very knowledgeable.

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:53.830
He won’t allow our underlings to
be thrown out onto the streets.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.120
I see.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:57.670
Don’t be saying what you please!

00:21:57.670 --> 00:22:01.050
We’d all consent to someone as
strong as you becoming our boss.

00:22:01.550 --> 00:22:03.260
I’d follow you all my life, Bro!

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:05.550
Don’t come near me!

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:07.810
Hey Kawachi, say something will you?!

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:08.560
Hmmm?

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:09.390
Kawachi!
Hmmm?

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:13.100
Hey, didn’t you tell me to shut up earlier?

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:14.190
Tsukino!

00:22:14.190 --> 00:22:15.110
Kanmuri!

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:16.940
The court chef, huh?

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.190
Awesome!

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:20.940
Then, how about we go sample some of my food?

00:22:20.950 --> 00:22:22.320
Oh, I’m envious!

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:22.950
I’d like to come too!

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:23.950
Please do.
I’d like to come too!

00:22:23.950 --> 00:22:24.740
G-Guys!

00:22:24.740 --> 00:22:25.160
Please, Bro!
G-Guys!

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:26.240
Please, Bro!

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:27.160
Well then, Bro, good to meet you.

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:27.950
Let’s all get along, shall we?
Well then, Bro, good to meet you.

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:28.740
Let’s all get along, shall we?

00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:32.710
A happy ending, huh?

00:22:32.710 --> 00:22:34.630
No it’s not!

00:22:53.930 --> 00:23:02.230
The world will probably go on today, with a repetition of the same faces,

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:10.280
but there was one thing that I’d forgotten.

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:15.050
If I’m to take a deep breath,

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:19.040
then the shape of the love that permeates my surroundings

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:26.630
will shine so much that it’s blinding.

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:35.010
Someone is calling me from far away...

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:43.400
And that voice constantly echoes in my heart.

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:51.990
So, riding on my small pleasures, the merry-go-round begins to turn...

00:23:51.990 --> 00:24:02.540
And even on days when the morning doesn’t come, it shines a light in my heart.

00:24:06.130 --> 00:24:07.520
Finally, he’s gonna come, you know...

00:24:07.520 --> 00:24:08.940
It’s amazing, you know...

00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:10.970
And it’s not a commercial, you know...

00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:12.970
Guys, you need to shut up, you know...

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:14.860
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:16.200
Seaweed bread showdown!!

00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:18.450
A really famous person is gonna appear, you know!

00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:19.980
Be sure to watch, okay?

00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:26.500
The history of jam dates way back to the days
of the Stone Age, more than 10,000 years ago.

00:24:26.500 --> 00:24:29.460
It originated when harvested fruits
were boiled down with honey.

00:24:29.460 --> 00:24:31.750
It is the oldest known way of preserving foodstuff.

00:24:32.250 --> 00:24:34.670
Oh?
